/**
@page targets Targets

@brief Building and running each build target, and porting to new hardware.

`libbotanik` builds for two targets from one codebase. The simulator runs it as a
Linux process; the firmware cross-compiles it for the OPTA. Both run the same site
verbatim - the only difference is who owns the PLC shared memory.

- @subpage md_src_2botanik__sim_2README - the Linux simulator (`SIMULATOR`):
  configure with CMake and run on the host. The harness allocates the shared region
  locally and drives a mock PLC.
- @subpage md_src_2botanik__fw_2README - the Arduino OPTA firmware (`OPTA`):
  cross-compile for the STM32H747 and deliver as an Arduino library zip. The real
  M4 coprocessor owns the shared region.
- @subpage porting - what a third target needs: a new HAL implementation behind the
  same interface.
*/
